   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend chapter 846 of the laws of 1970, amending the county law relating to payment in lieu of taxes for property acquired for park or recreational purposes, in relation to extending the term of effectiveness of such chapter",
    "basePrintNo": "S6432",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S6432-2009",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §2, Chap 846 of 1970",
    "lawSection": "Parks",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S6432\n\n TITLE OF BILL :\nAn act to amend chapter 846 of the laws of 1970, amending the county\nlaw relating to payment in lieu of taxes for property acquired for\npark or recreational purposes, in relation to extending the term of\neffectiveness of such chapter\n\n\n PURPOSE :\nTo extend until June 30, 2015 the authorization to Nassau County to\nmake payments in lieu of taxes on certain parklands in Lido\nBeach-Point Lookout area.\n\n SUMMARY OF PROVISIONS :\nSection 2 of Chapter 846 of the Law of 1970 amending the County law is\namended as it pertains to the payment in lieu of taxes by Nassau\nCounty to certain districts in the Lido Beach area by extending its\ntermination date from June 30, 2010 to June 30, 2015.\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\nThe Long Beach City School District has reached its constitutional tax\nlimit so that these payments have now become crucial to its fiscal\nwell-being. Similar bills extending this legislation have been passed\nand signed into law on five prior occasions (1975-80, 1980-85,\n1985-90, 1990-95, 1995-2000, 2000-2005, 2005-2010.)\n\n LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\nChapter 130 of the Laws of 2005\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\nNone to State.\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
